<html><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><style>
body{font-family:Calibri,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:#111827;line-height:1.7;max-width:860px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 28px}
h1{font-size:22pt;color:#111827;border-bottom:3px solid #c5a028;padding-bottom:8px;margin-bottom:4px}
h2{font-size:14pt;color:#111827;margin-top:30px;margin-bottom:4px;border-left:4px solid #4fd1c5;padding-left:12px;background:#f4fdfc}
h3{font-size:12pt;color:#374151;margin:16px 0 4px;font-weight:bold}
p{margin:4px 0 10px}
.meta{background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:6px;padding:14px 18px;margin-bottom:24px;font-size:10pt}
.meta p{margin:3px 0}
.meta strong{color:#b7881c}
.sec{border-top:1px solid #e5e7eb;margin-top:28px;padding-top:16px}
.badge{display:inline-block;background:#ecfdf5;color:#065f46;font-size:9pt;font-weight:bold;padding:3px 12px;border-radius:20px;margin-bottom:8px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px}
.card{background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:8px;padding:14px 16px;margin:10px 0}
.card-title{font-weight:bold;font-size:11.5pt;color:#111827;margin:0 0 4px}
.card-sub{font-size:10pt;color:#6b7280;margin:0 0 4px;font-style:italic}
.card-desc{color:#374151;margin:0;font-size:10.5pt}
.step{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;padding:12px 14px;background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:8px;margin:8px 0}
.step-num{font-size:18pt;font-weight:bold;color:#c5a028;min-width:40px;line-height:1}
.step-body .step-title{font-weight:bold;font-size:11pt;color:#111827;margin:0 0 3px}
.step-body .step-desc{font-size:10.5pt;color:#374151;margin:0}
.faq{border-left:3px solid #4fd1c5;padding:10px 14px;margin:12px 0;background:#f9fafb;border-radius:0 6px 6px 0}
.faq-q{font-weight:bold;color:#111827;margin:0 0 5px}
.faq-a{color:#374151;margin:0;font-size:10.5pt}
.cta{background:#111827;color:#fff;border-radius:10px;padding:20px 24px;margin-top:28px}
.cta h2{color:#4fd1c5;border:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 8px;background:transparent;font-size:15pt}
.cta p{color:#d1d5db;margin:4px 0}
.cta .btn{display:inline-block;background:#4fd1c5;color:#111827;font-weight:bold;padding:7px 16px;border-radius:5px;margin-top:8px;font-size:10pt}
table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:10px 0;font-size:10.5pt}
td{padding:7px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb}
td:first-child{color:#6b7280}
td:last-child{font-weight:bold;color:#111827;text-align:right}
ul{padding-left:18px}
ul li{padding:2px 0;color:#374151}
</style></head><body><h1>First Time Home Buyers</h1><div class="meta"><p><strong>Page Title:</strong> First-Time Home Buyer Programs Madison, WI | Rob Miller | MadCity</p><p><strong>Meta Description:</strong> Expert guidance for first-time homebuyers in Wisconsin. Low down payments, WHEDA assistance, and 5-star service from Rob Miller. Licensed in 11 states. Call 608-227-2002.</p></div><div class="sec"><h2>Benefits</h2><div class="card"><p class="card-title">WHEDA Advantage</p><p class="card-desc">Wisconsin's state program offers below-market rates + up to 6% down payment assistance exclusively for WI residents.</p></div><div class="card"><p class="card-title">FHA Loans</p><p class="card-desc">As little as 3.5% down with a 580+ credit score. Gift funds from family are allowed for the entire down payment.</p></div><div class="card"><p class="card-title">Conventional 97</p><p class="card-desc">Fannie Mae HomeReady and Freddie Mac Home Possible offer 3% down for first-time buyers with income limits.</p></div><div class="card"><p class="card-title">VA Loans (Veterans)</p><p class="card-desc">$0 down with no PMI for eligible veterans and active-duty service members — the most powerful first-time buyer tool available.</p></div><div class="card"><p class="card-title">USDA Loans</p><p class="card-desc">$0 down for eligible suburban and rural Wisconsin properties. Broader geographic coverage than most buyers realize.</p></div><div class="card"><p class="card-title">Down Payment Assistance</p><p class="card-desc">WHEDA Easy Close DPA provides up to 6% of purchase price. Additional local programs may be available in your area.</p></div></div><div class="sec"><h2>Process Roadmap</h2><div class="step"><div class="step-num">01</div><div class="step-body"><p class="step-title">Get Pre-Approved</p><p class="step-desc">Know your budget before you start shopping. A pre-approval letter also makes your offers competitive.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">02</div><div class="step-body"><p class="step-title">Identify Your Program</p><p class="step-desc">Rob reviews your credit, income, and savings to identify every program you qualify for and rank them by total cost.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">03</div><div class="step-body"><p class="step-title">Complete Homebuyer Education</p><p class="step-desc">WHEDA and some DPA programs require an online course — typically 6–8 hours and available anytime.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">04</div><div class="step-body"><p class="step-title">Make an Offer</p><p class="step-desc">Your agent submits the offer; your pre-approval letter is attached to show sellers you're a serious, qualified buyer.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">05</div><div class="step-body"><p class="step-title">Application & Underwriting</p><p class="step-desc">Rob's team handles the loan processing, keeps you updated, and resolves any underwriting conditions quickly.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">06</div><div class="step-body"><p class="step-title">Close & Get Your Keys</p><p class="step-desc">Sign your closing documents, pay your minimal down payment and closing costs, and get your keys.</p></div></div></div><div class="sec"><h2>Hero Section</h2><h3>YOUR FIRST HOME. MADE SIMPLE.</h3><p>Buying your first home is the biggest financial decision of your life. Rob Miller has spent 20+ years simplifying the process for Wisconsin buyers with down payment assistance, low rates, and five-star service.</p></div><div class="sec"><h2>Main Page Content</h2><h3>Buying in Wisconsin</h3><h3>Buyer Programs</h3><h3>Your Roadmap</h3><h4>First-Time Buyer Options</h4><p>The biggest barrier for most first-time buyers isn't income — it's the upfront cost. Down payments, closing costs, inspections, and moving expenses can add up fast. The good news: Wisconsin has some of the best first-time homebuyer programs in the country, and Rob Miller knows how to stack them to minimize what you need to bring to closing.</p><p>Whether you're buying in Madison, Middleton, Sun Prairie, Fitchburg, or anywhere in Wisconsin, the right combination of loan program and assistance can make homeownership far more achievable than you think — often with less cash out of pocket than your current monthly rent.</p><p>Not sure which program is right for you? A free 15-minute call with Rob Miller is all it takes to find out exactly what you qualify for and how much you'll need at closing.</p></div><div class="sec"><h2>First-Time Buyer Options</h2><table><tr><td>Lowest Down Payment</td><td>$0 (VA/USDA)</td></tr><tr><td>FHA Minimum</td><td>3.5%</td></tr><tr><td>Conventional Min.</td><td>3%</td></tr><tr><td>WHEDA DPA</td><td>Up to 6%</td></tr><tr><td>Min. Credit Score</td><td>500 (FHA)</td></tr><tr><td>Avg. Close Time</td><td>30–45 days</td></tr></table></div><div class="sec"><h2>First-Time Buyer FAQs — Wisconsin</h2><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: What qualifies as a "first-time homebuyer" in Wisconsin?</p><p class="faq-a">A: For most programs, a first-time homebuyer is someone who has not owned a primary residence in the past 3 years. This means if you previously owned a home but sold it 3+ years ago, you may qualify as a first-time buyer again. Veterans and buyers in certain WHEDA-targeted areas may be exempt from the first-time buyer requirement.</p></div><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: What is the minimum down payment for a first-time buyer?</p><p class="faq-a">A: As little as $0 with VA or USDA loans for eligible buyers. WHEDA and FHA programs start at 3% and 3.5% respectively. Conventional HomeReady and Home Possible programs allow 3% down for first-time buyers. Rob Miller will identify the lowest-down-payment option you qualify for.</p></div><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: Is down payment assistance available in Wisconsin?</p><p class="faq-a">A: Yes — WHEDA's Easy Close DPA program provides up to 6% of the purchase price as a low-interest second mortgage for down payment and closing costs. Some local municipalities and nonprofits also offer additional assistance. Rob Miller knows the local programs available in Madison, Dane County, and across Wisconsin.</p></div><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: Do I need to take a homebuyer education course?</p><p class="faq-a">A: WHEDA loans require completion of an approved homebuyer education course, which is available online. Some other first-time buyer programs also require it. The course typically takes 6–8 hours and covers budgeting, the buying process, and maintaining your home. Many buyers find it genuinely useful.</p></div><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: What credit score do I need to buy my first home?</p><p class="faq-a">A: It depends on the loan program. FHA allows scores as low as 580 (with 3.5% down) or 500 (with 10% down). Conventional loans require 620+. WHEDA requires 620+. VA and USDA don't set a minimum, but most lenders require 580–640. Rob Miller works with first-time buyers at every credit level to find viable paths forward.</p></div><div class="faq"><p class="faq-q">Q: How long does it take to buy a first home in Wisconsin?</p><p class="faq-a">A: From starting your search to closing day, the typical Wisconsin homebuying process takes 60–90 days. The mortgage process itself — from application to closing — typically runs 30–45 days once you're under contract. Getting pre-approved before you start shopping puts you in the best position to move quickly when you find your home.</p></div></div><div class="cta"><h2>Ready to Buy Your First Home in Wisconsin?</h2><p>Rob Miller has helped hundreds of first-time buyers in Madison and across Wisconsin. Let</p><span class="btn">Get My Free Pre-Approval</span></div></body></html>